{
  "about": "Product terms and how each language says them, one set for every Vibefork product. `address` is the form of address per language. A term with `match` (a JavaScript regular expression, case-insensitive unless `caseSensitive`) is checked: where the English text matches it, the text in each other language contains one of `expect` (case-insensitive). A term without `match` is for translators only. `forbidden` spellings appear in no text. Keys a product exempts from a term live in that product, not here.",
  "address": {
    "en": "you",
    "ru": "вы",
    "pt-BR": "você",
    "es-ES": "tú",
    "es-419": "tú",
    "de": "du"
  },
  "forbidden": [
    "VibeFork",
    "Vibe Fork"
  ],
